Coach Cal went on to say that the 14-time Grammy winner was just a few feet away from him, at one point conversing with Adam Sandler and his wife. Despite knowing the Happy Gilmore star, the Basketball Hall of Famer said he was &#8220;intimidated&#8221; to approach.

&#8220;She came up and was bubbly, and then I&#8217;m sitting here at this table,&#8221; he added. &#8220;She&#8217;s at other end &#8230; I took my phone and I acted like I was on my phone, and I wasn&#8217;t on my phone, but I acted like I was.&#8221;

To underscore how big of a deal it was, Calipari also shared that the last time he felt nearly as starstruck by a powerful figure was when he met Barack Obama &#8212; and even then, he had no problem shaking the president&#8217;s hand.

Swift notably attended two Knicks games this year. She first went with then-fiancé Travis Kelce to the New York team&#8217;s away game against the Cleveland Cavaliers in May. It was just a couple of weeks later that she cheered on the Knicks &#8212; who&#8217;d go on to win the NBA Finals &#8212; at MSG, sitting next to Mariska Hargitay and Este and Alana Haim.

Less than a month after that, Swift would return to MSG for her wedding, which Sandler officiated. The pop star is now fresh off the release of her The Life of a Showgirl: The Encore deluxe, which earned her a 16th career No. 1 on the Billboard Hot 100 with &#8220;Patient Zero.&#8221;
